WEBVTT

00:01.070 --> 00:04.580
The Pocket Monsters XY&Z 1 Hour Special!

00:05.860 --> 00:07.110
The conclusion will be tonight!

00:07.250 --> 00:11.060
His goal is to destroy the world

00:07.280 --> 00:08.150
The curtain rises...

00:09.130 --> 00:11.060
Fleur-de-lis plans to destroy the world.

00:12.220 --> 00:16.000
His collaborator Alan realizes that he was being used...

00:17.250 --> 00:17.990
I'll stop the director.

00:18.680 --> 00:19.830
That's the spirit.

00:20.290 --> 00:23.870
They go up against Fleur-de-lis

00:21.100 --> 00:23.260
...and goes up against Fleur-de-lis together with Satoshi.

00:24.240 --> 00:27.500
Fleur-de-lis VS Satoshi & Alan

00:24.370 --> 00:25.410
Let's go, everyone!

00:27.670 --> 00:30.810
The biggest crisis in the history of Kalos

00:30.960 --> 00:32.400
Aim at the Water Shuriken!

00:33.950 --> 00:38.150
Save the world!

00:34.220 --> 00:35.100
Satoshi, Alan!

00:35.510 --> 00:37.500
Save the world with everyone's help!

00:38.470 --> 00:38.960
And then...!

00:39.260 --> 00:40.350
Let us show you...

00:40.640 --> 00:42.490
...our full power!

00:42.690 --> 00:48.020
Zygarde 100% Forme!

00:43.370 --> 00:47.140
Finally, Zygarde's Perfect Forme shows itself!

00:48.020 --> 00:49.360
I will...

00:50.130 --> 00:51.080
...destroy the world.

00:51.980 --> 00:55.160
Now, will Satoshi be able to save the world?

00:52.070 --> 00:59.870
Can Satoshi save the world!?

00:56.340 --> 00:58.930
Let the Pokémon 1 Hour Special start!

01:02.040 --> 01:11.880
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

01:02.880 --> 01:05.620
The Flare Gang has brought about the destruction of Kalos.

01:07.140 --> 01:11.100
Together with Manon, Serena has successfully rescued Harimaron.

01:13.200 --> 01:22.560
In order to stop Squishy, Eureka confronted the rampaging Squishy together with Burshamo Mask and broke the mind control.

01:25.620 --> 01:33.640
Finally, Citron and the Citroid destroyed the Flare Gang's mind system and successfully set Zygarde free.

01:36.080 --> 01:41.910
However, that turned out to be a cruel trade-off that cost the Citroid its memory.

01:46.560 --> 01:49.160
Meanwhile, Satoshi and Alan...

01:50.310 --> 01:51.720
Hyper Beam!

01:53.010 --> 01:54.610
Pikachu, Quick Attack!

01:57.160 --> 01:57.780
Don't give it time to recover!

01:58.160 --> 01:58.900
Dragon Claw!

01:59.110 --> 02:00.560
Gekkouga, Cut!

02:06.560 --> 02:08.090
Go, Thunderbolt!

02:21.570 --> 02:25.260
That "brutality" and "fighting instinct" of yours have been defeated.

02:25.860 --> 02:27.160
It's over, Fleur-de-lis.

02:30.570 --> 02:31.670
Something like this...

02:33.380 --> 02:35.920
...won't end my desires.

02:39.540 --> 02:41.980
I will change the world.

02:44.090 --> 02:44.770
Gekkouga!

02:51.400 --> 02:51.840
Fleur-de-lis!

03:08.110 --> 03:08.700
Satoshi?

03:09.110 --> 03:09.670
Serena,

03:09.960 --> 03:10.820
where are you?

03:11.580 --> 03:14.640
We've just rescued Hari-san from the Fleur-de-lis Labs.

03:15.860 --> 03:18.830
Manon, Professor Platane and Daigo-san are here with me as well.

03:19.360 --> 03:19.670
Manon!

03:20.410 --> 03:21.170
Manon, you're there too?

03:21.760 --> 03:22.820
I'm here, Alan.

03:23.370 --> 03:24.460
Alan, are you all right?

03:24.920 --> 03:25.280
Yeah.

03:25.990 --> 03:26.450
What about you, Manon?

03:26.870 --> 03:27.330
Yeah.

03:27.510 --> 03:28.610
Hari-san is safe too.

03:29.840 --> 03:30.940
I'm so glad for you, Alan.

03:31.750 --> 03:33.010
Satoshi, where are you?

03:33.700 --> 03:35.840
Right now, we're at the top of the Prism Tower.

03:36.680 --> 03:38.500
In that case, can you drop by the Gym?

03:39.400 --> 03:40.070
Citron is...

03:45.310 --> 03:51.020
The Megalith Advances!
Kalos' Defense Line!!

03:53.460 --> 03:54.370
Sludge Bomb!

03:54.370 --> 03:55.300
Ice Beam!

03:57.500 --> 03:59.010
I'm counting on you, Sonansu!

04:05.710 --> 04:06.380
Now, Kojiro!

04:06.590 --> 04:07.460
String Shot!

04:07.590 --> 04:09.620
I'm not a Bug type...

04:11.020 --> 04:13.020
Hey, let me go!

04:13.600 --> 04:14.200
Oh my...

04:16.140 --> 04:17.890
Flare Gang, you're under arrest.

04:19.090 --> 04:28.930
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

04:19.090 --> 04:28.930
Z

04:24.050 --> 04:25.170
What are you doing?

04:25.700 --> 04:28.620
I'm checking what they were researching here.

04:32.710 --> 04:33.200
This is...!

04:35.020 --> 04:35.530
Is something wrong?

04:42.060 --> 04:42.390
Huh?

04:45.180 --> 04:45.620
What?

04:54.370 --> 04:54.770
Hari-san!

04:56.780 --> 04:57.530
Hey!

05:00.900 --> 05:01.710
Hari-san!

05:02.140 --> 05:03.160
Wait, Manon-kun!

05:04.230 --> 05:04.510
But...

05:05.930 --> 05:07.350
...Hari-san is gonna disappear!

05:08.130 --> 05:08.720
It's dangerous!

05:14.670 --> 05:15.480
Hari-san!

05:16.040 --> 05:17.500
Hari-san!

05:17.620 --> 05:18.180
Manon-kun!

05:18.620 --> 05:19.720
Let's run for now!

05:33.580 --> 05:34.140
Hari-san...

05:36.280 --> 05:36.720
Professor...

05:37.200 --> 05:37.740
What's going on?

05:38.680 --> 05:39.410
I don't know.

05:39.990 --> 05:41.500
I had no idea the megalith had this kind of power.

05:41.850 --> 05:42.220
No.

05:43.000 --> 05:44.930
The megalith <i>itself</i> is the power.

05:46.010 --> 05:47.930
Nothing would surprise me now.

05:53.740 --> 05:54.460
Wha-wha-wha-wha?!

05:54.810 --> 05:55.930
What is that?!

05:55.930 --> 05:57.300
This is our chance for a scoop!

05:58.360 --> 06:00.190
Who will do it if not us?

06:01.060 --> 06:03.190
The world is waiting for the truth!

06:03.980 --> 06:06.060
We have to inform the world of this danger!

06:06.060 --> 06:08.430
We have to deliver information to the world!

06:08.430 --> 06:11.020
Carrying out coverage of love and truth,

06:11.020 --> 06:13.300
we're lovely, charmy TV people.

06:13.300 --> 06:14.110
Musashi!

06:14.110 --> 06:14.460
Kojiro!

06:15.120 --> 06:18.060
For the Rocket Gang duo delivering live broadcasts...

06:18.450 --> 06:21.080
...a white hole, a white tomorrow awaits ahead!

06:21.530 --> 06:22.780
Just kidding!

06:34.930 --> 06:36.610
The sundial is frightened.

06:42.520 --> 06:43.480
Citron!

06:54.390 --> 06:55.460
What happened?

06:57.990 --> 06:59.030
It was thanks to him.

07:03.820 --> 07:04.840
He can be fixed, right?

07:05.800 --> 07:06.700
I <i>will</i> fix him.

07:08.330 --> 07:09.130
I still have not...

07:09.700 --> 07:11.720
...been able to do anything for him, after all.

07:16.700 --> 07:17.190
Serena...

07:17.530 --> 07:18.640
Ah, Satoshi!

07:19.010 --> 07:19.690
We're in trouble!

07:20.090 --> 07:22.980
Harimaron has been sucked into the megalith at the Fleur-de-lis Labs!

07:24.390 --> 07:25.440
Harimaron has?

07:26.590 --> 07:28.850
That megalith is now moving towards somewhere.

07:29.970 --> 07:31.770
We don't know where it's heading.

07:32.380 --> 07:33.610
We'll send you info on its current location.

07:34.220 --> 07:35.240
Please head there with Burshamo Mask.

07:36.330 --> 07:38.650
We're going to keep pursuing and analyzing it.

07:39.200 --> 07:40.460
Satoshi, be careful!

07:41.190 --> 07:41.500
I will.

07:43.690 --> 07:44.170
Citron...

07:47.960 --> 07:48.690
I am all right.

07:50.940 --> 07:52.540
The fight is not over yet.

08:04.830 --> 08:05.550
Good evening.

08:05.990 --> 08:07.470
You're Squishy's friend, right?

08:11.600 --> 08:13.740
Take in this terrible sight.

08:14.920 --> 08:17.030
Humans did this.

08:17.980 --> 08:19.260
This is why humans...!

08:20.020 --> 08:21.750
We believe in humans.

08:22.820 --> 08:24.250
Why are you still...?

08:25.860 --> 08:28.470
Because we haven't given up on humans yet.

08:34.380 --> 08:34.770
Come on.

08:35.100 --> 08:35.490
Come here.

08:36.050 --> 08:36.760
No need to be scared.

08:37.990 --> 08:38.810
Let's go together!

08:42.580 --> 08:42.770
This eye has...

08:43.580 --> 08:45.150
...witnessed many things...

08:46.130 --> 08:48.440
...through traveling with this girl and her friends.

08:49.890 --> 08:50.660
They have helped each other,

08:51.800 --> 08:52.560
worked hard together,

08:53.330 --> 08:54.190
experienced joy,

08:55.060 --> 08:55.840
believed in each other,

08:56.880 --> 08:57.520
strived for a goal,

08:58.340 --> 08:59.040
moved forward...

08:59.800 --> 09:00.620
...and...

09:01.170 --> 09:03.680
...never gave up.

09:07.320 --> 09:08.740
If you're Squishy's friend,

09:09.150 --> 09:10.170
I'm your friend too!

09:11.090 --> 09:11.940
I won't do anything to you.

09:12.700 --> 09:13.520
Let's get along!

09:16.770 --> 09:17.260
That's right.

09:19.190 --> 09:22.460
Squishy likes it when I do this to this spot.

09:33.430 --> 09:34.300
Everyone, please listen.

09:35.060 --> 09:37.540
We will tell you what we know about that megalith.

09:38.800 --> 09:40.440
We've scanned that megalith.

09:41.080 --> 09:43.400
It's all an incredible mass of energy.

09:43.990 --> 09:46.960
Its energy resembles that of Zygarde.

09:47.790 --> 09:51.510
Also, we have detected vital signs from Harimaron from its core.

09:52.240 --> 09:56.220
There were records on Harimaron in the data we got at the Fleur-de-lis Labs.

09:57.020 --> 10:02.330
According to them, it seems Harimaron once got into an accident that filled its body with Zygarde's energy.

10:03.970 --> 10:05.960
We can assume that the megalith...

10:06.780 --> 10:09.020
...absorbed Harimaron whole to get that energy.

10:09.930 --> 10:13.240
Even worse, the megalith wants even more energy.

10:17.210 --> 10:17.910
This is...

10:18.550 --> 10:19.280
...Hyakkoku City.

10:19.840 --> 10:20.840
Hyakkoku City?

10:22.620 --> 10:24.290
It's heading straight towards the sundial.

10:25.650 --> 10:29.210
The sundial is a huge crystal that is said to have come flying from space.

10:30.230 --> 10:37.340
We know that the energy it emits is the same as the energy unleashed when a Pokémon mega evolves.

10:38.570 --> 10:41.050
Let's say the megalith is striving to obtain that energy.

10:41.800 --> 10:43.150
<i>Why</i> is it doing that?

10:43.650 --> 10:44.170
This is why.

10:45.800 --> 10:49.970
If that megalith and the sundial were to meet and fuse...

10:58.860 --> 10:59.660
Does that mean...?

11:00.670 --> 11:02.490
It's the end of our world.

11:04.250 --> 11:06.930
The director wants to destroy this world <i>this</i> badly...

11:07.420 --> 11:08.960
We won't let him do this.

11:09.810 --> 11:10.330
Professor,

11:10.750 --> 11:13.790
we will save Harimaron and stop the megalith.

11:15.240 --> 11:15.880
We...

11:16.420 --> 11:17.040
...can do it!

11:19.140 --> 11:19.660
Satoshi...

11:20.130 --> 11:20.890
We'll be waiting.

11:21.410 --> 11:21.790
Okay.

11:25.430 --> 11:25.760
Manon.

11:27.880 --> 11:28.380
I promise...

11:29.240 --> 11:31.100
...I'll save Harimaron, for sure.

11:32.810 --> 11:33.160
Okay.

11:35.580 --> 11:36.520
Pokémon Quiz.

11:37.140 --> 11:37.980
The answer is...

11:40.060 --> 11:55.010
Coming up next:

11:40.060 --> 11:47.530
Stop the megalith! Save the world!

11:40.730 --> 11:44.390
This program is brought to you by these sponsors.

11:47.570 --> 11:55.010
The ones who come to Satoshi and Alan's rescue are...!!

12:05.900 --> 12:08.140
That's all the information I got from Professor Platane.

12:09.500 --> 12:12.140
You go and evacuate the residents of Hyakkoku, hurry.

12:12.720 --> 12:12.910
Okay.

12:14.680 --> 12:16.460
We shall not let them destroy the sundial.

12:19.790 --> 12:20.470
Gather!

12:26.360 --> 12:30.100
The strange huge object is currently moving towards Hyakkoku City.

12:30.630 --> 12:33.310
Local residents, please evacuate quickly.

12:40.190 --> 12:41.030
Are you ready?

12:41.530 --> 12:41.780
Yes.

12:42.640 --> 12:43.910
We will fight, too!

12:44.730 --> 12:45.400
Serena...

12:45.980 --> 12:47.150
We've got to do this!

12:47.990 --> 12:49.450
I don't want the world...

12:49.850 --> 12:50.930
...to just end like this!

12:52.800 --> 12:54.160
Go, Metagross!

12:54.590 --> 12:55.980
Go, Gablias!

12:56.740 --> 12:57.990
Please, Tairenar!

13:04.830 --> 13:05.830
Mega evolve!

13:23.970 --> 13:24.710
Flash Cannon!

13:25.050 --> 13:25.810
Dragon Pulse!

13:26.170 --> 13:26.980
Flamethrower!

13:37.370 --> 13:38.190
Dragon Pulse!

13:41.430 --> 13:42.150
Flamethrower!

13:42.150 --> 13:42.860
Flash Cannon!

13:47.310 --> 13:48.560
It's the brat girl and the others!

13:52.320 --> 13:52.940
Gablias!

13:58.070 --> 13:58.870
Tairenar!

13:58.870 --> 13:59.350
Metagross!

14:06.540 --> 14:07.360
Lizardon...

14:07.660 --> 14:08.360
...and Pikachu!

14:16.010 --> 14:16.640
Satoshi!

14:17.000 --> 14:17.610
Citron!

14:18.100 --> 14:18.690
Alan!

14:21.650 --> 14:22.800
There they are.

14:22.800 --> 14:24.370
Now the cast is assembled.

14:26.360 --> 14:27.790
Lizardon, Flamethrower!

14:28.020 --> 14:29.540
Pikachu, Iron Tail!

14:45.800 --> 14:51.290
In an attempt to prevent the strange huge object from advancing, Professor Platane and a group of additional bra-

14:51.510 --> 14:55.220
I mean, <i>Pokémon Trainers</i>, keep fighting it.

14:56.730 --> 14:57.440
Satoshi...

15:06.880 --> 15:07.340
Professor,

15:07.820 --> 15:09.840
do you know Hari-san's concrete location?

15:10.490 --> 15:12.950
The scan only showed that it's near the center.

15:29.990 --> 15:30.540
Gekkouga,

15:31.100 --> 15:32.070
did you see it too?

15:33.700 --> 15:34.220
All right.

15:34.670 --> 15:35.670
I have an idea.

15:36.280 --> 15:37.250
Let's do this, Gekkouga.

15:40.580 --> 15:41.040
Satoshi-kun,

15:41.620 --> 15:42.530
will you be all right?

15:43.060 --> 15:43.380
Yes.

15:44.050 --> 15:45.330
Please trust us.

15:52.830 --> 15:54.950
Pikachu, back up Gekkouga!

15:55.430 --> 15:56.920
Lizardon, you too!

15:57.810 --> 15:59.080
Assist Satoshi-kun and the others!

15:59.420 --> 16:00.700
Metagross, I'm counting on you!

16:04.970 --> 16:05.420
Hari-san...

16:05.910 --> 16:07.680
Please be safe.

16:27.140 --> 16:27.540
Found it.

16:28.090 --> 16:28.710
Gekkouga,

16:28.950 --> 16:29.980
Water Shuriken!

16:34.990 --> 16:35.600
There it is.

16:36.160 --> 16:37.820
Hari-san is behind that shuriken.

16:39.010 --> 16:39.510
Everyone!

16:39.830 --> 16:41.220
Aim at the Water Shuriken!

16:42.870 --> 16:43.230
Right!

16:55.000 --> 16:56.550
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

17:01.330 --> 17:02.230
Flamethrower!

17:09.390 --> 17:10.370
Hyper Beam!

17:13.640 --> 17:14.620
Flash Cannon!

17:16.370 --> 17:17.420
Flamethrower!

17:20.400 --> 17:21.390
There's no end to them.

17:22.170 --> 17:24.140
We're never going to reach the main body like this!

17:27.910 --> 17:28.980
Use Cut!

17:37.810 --> 17:38.680
Pikachu!

17:38.920 --> 17:39.360
Lizardon!

17:43.980 --> 17:44.790
Tairenar!

17:44.790 --> 17:45.410
Metagross!

17:48.370 --> 17:49.070
Gablias!

17:49.850 --> 17:51.170
Hey, they're in trouble!

17:51.170 --> 17:51.700
What now?

18:00.310 --> 18:01.420
What? What?!

18:14.640 --> 18:15.730
What?!

18:23.560 --> 18:24.230
Everyone!

18:24.420 --> 18:25.830
It is the Gym Leaders!

18:26.540 --> 18:27.620
Awesome!

18:28.620 --> 18:29.730
That was close.

18:31.810 --> 18:32.980
Satoshi, sorry to keep you waiting!

18:33.240 --> 18:35.000
Gym Leader of the Shala Gym, Corni

18:35.650 --> 18:38.260
Doesn't look like it's going to stop if we ask it to.

18:39.500 --> 18:41.210
Kalos Champion,
Carne

18:41.600 --> 18:42.930
It sure is huge.

18:43.420 --> 18:45.260
Make sure not to be a burden, Zakuro-kun.

18:45.470 --> 18:47.220
Gym Leader of the Hakudan Gym, Viola

18:47.690 --> 18:48.420
Right, right.

18:49.050 --> 18:51.260
But really though, that wall <i>is</i> extremely good for climbing.

18:51.470 --> 18:53.220
Gym Leader of
the Shoyo Gym,
Zakuro

18:53.740 --> 18:55.270
Those plants are strong.

18:55.820 --> 18:58.070
Let us brace ourselves, Gogoat.

18:58.480 --> 19:00.230
Gym Leader of the Hiyoku Gym,
Fukuji

19:00.930 --> 19:02.870
It's full of negative energy.

19:03.480 --> 19:05.240
Gym Leader of
the Kunoe Gym,
Mâche

19:06.470 --> 19:08.480
We cannot let it meet the sundial.

19:09.490 --> 19:11.240
Gym Leader of the Hyakkoku Gym, Gojika

19:11.870 --> 19:13.070
That means... you know.

19:13.490 --> 19:15.600
We should use our full power right from the start, huh?

19:15.750 --> 19:17.750
Gym Leader of the Eisetsu Gym,
Urup

19:23.780 --> 19:25.700
I can't believe that didn't even buy us any time.

19:27.150 --> 19:29.210
Let's withdraw for the time being and think of a plan.

19:33.800 --> 19:34.890
I understand the situation.

19:35.720 --> 19:37.410
Hari-san's rescue takes top priority.

19:38.530 --> 19:38.740
Yes.

19:39.740 --> 19:42.690
Let's use our Pokémon's moves to break into the megalith itself.

19:43.760 --> 19:44.650
What marks the spot is that...

19:45.210 --> 19:45.880
...Water Shuriken.

19:51.430 --> 19:52.990
Let's combine our powers and fight.

19:53.790 --> 19:57.200
I'm honored to be fighting alongside you, Carne-san.

19:58.110 --> 19:59.710
Likewise, Daigo-san.

20:00.950 --> 20:02.970
We couldn't have asked for stronger allies.

20:03.980 --> 20:04.540
Satoshi!

20:04.910 --> 20:05.240
Corni!

20:05.850 --> 20:07.370
So <i>that's</i> the Gekkouga I've heard about.

20:07.870 --> 20:08.310
Yeah.

20:08.710 --> 20:10.280
This is me and Gekkouga's power.

20:10.800 --> 20:11.530
Awesome!

20:12.350 --> 20:14.720
So you've finally obtained that power.

20:15.360 --> 20:15.680
Yes.

20:21.880 --> 20:22.460
Guys!

20:22.980 --> 20:24.730
This is the final line of defense.

20:25.430 --> 20:27.700
We cannot let it crash into the sundial no matter what.

20:28.460 --> 20:29.750
Please approach it with care.

20:30.160 --> 20:30.780
Yeah!

20:32.710 --> 20:33.820
Let's go, Hellgar.

20:35.670 --> 20:36.160
Serena!

20:36.550 --> 20:38.180
Please protect Manon and Eureka.

20:39.100 --> 20:40.500
I am counting on you, Serena.

20:41.010 --> 20:41.450
Got it!

20:41.830 --> 20:42.420
Leave it to me.

20:43.400 --> 20:44.940
Bro, Satoshi, be careful!

20:46.550 --> 20:47.190
Alan...

20:48.220 --> 20:48.730
It'll be fine.

20:49.590 --> 20:51.190
I will bring Harimaron back, no matter what.

20:52.290 --> 20:52.570
Okay.

20:59.000 --> 21:00.720
Nyarth, make sure to get good footage!

21:00.990 --> 21:02.130
Leave it to me!

21:03.000 --> 21:05.730
People all over the world, please look at this!

21:06.050 --> 21:09.130
Those people are taking responsibility for handling the Kalos crisis!

21:11.930 --> 21:16.780
In order to rescue Harimaron, and to prevent the sundial and megalith from colliding,

21:17.190 --> 21:20.790
the strongest team of Kalos has gathered and is now joining the fight.

21:21.830 --> 21:23.060
What is Hari-san's fate?

21:23.570 --> 21:24.800
What will become of the future of Kalos?

21:25.320 --> 21:27.060
The final battle takes place in the next episode!

21:34.710 --> 21:36.050
Pokémon Twenty Four Hours!

21:36.770 --> 21:39.970
All right! Today, we'll present the Gym Leaders of the Kalos region!

21:40.810 --> 21:42.160
She never misses a good photo opportunity:

21:42.460 --> 21:43.770
Viola of the Hakudan Gym!

21:44.880 --> 21:46.750
He can be found wherever there's a wall:

21:47.140 --> 21:48.590
Zakuro of the Shoyo Gym!

21:49.830 --> 21:50.680
She explodes with life!

21:51.050 --> 21:53.390
The martial artist with spirit: Corni of the Shala Gym!

21:54.420 --> 21:56.220
A big tree who makes flowers of hope bloom:

21:56.550 --> 21:57.770
Fukuji of the Hiyoku Gym!

21:58.970 --> 22:00.210
The danseuse of the Fairy world:

22:00.510 --> 22:01.980
Mâche of the Kunoe Gym!

22:03.300 --> 22:04.370
The mesmerizing seer:

22:04.770 --> 22:06.160
Gojika of the Hyakkoku Gym!

22:07.690 --> 22:08.960
The hot-blooded blizzard:

22:09.120 --> 22:10.700
Urup of the Eisetsu Gym!

22:12.410 --> 22:13.870
The steely electric cyborg:

22:14.160 --> 22:15.560
The Citroid of the Miare Gym!

22:17.040 --> 22:19.180
These Gym Leaders sure are dependable, aren't they?

22:19.610 --> 22:22.450
They're awaiting challenges from you Trainers!

22:22.450 --> 22:25.550
Do not forget about me!

22:26.820 --> 22:29.980
Zygarde's Perfect Forme will appear right after this!
